.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_SET0_CA_LIST 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_set_client_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_get_client_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_get_client_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_add_client_CA ,
.Nm SSL_add_client_CA ,
.Nm SSL_set0_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set0_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_get0_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_get0_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_add1_to_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_add1_to_CA_list ,
.Nm SSL_get0_peer_CA_list
.Nd get or set CA list
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509_NAME) *list"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_set_client_CA_list
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509_NAME) *list"
.Fc
.Bd -literal
 STACK_OF(X509_NAME) *SSL_get_client_CA_list(const SSL *s);
 STACK_OF(X509_NAME) *SSL_CTX_get_client_CA_list(const SSL_CTX *ctx);
 int SSL_CTX_add_client_CA(SSL_CTX *ctx, X509 *cacert);
 int SSL_add_client_CA(SSL *ssl, X509 *cacert);
.Ed
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set0_CA_list
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509_NAME) *name_list"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_set0_CA_list
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509_NAME) *name_list"
.Fc
.Ft const
.Fo STACK_OF
.Fa X509_NAME
.Fc
 *SSL_CTX_get0_CA_list(const SSL_CTX *ctx);
.Ft const
.Fo STACK_OF
.Fa X509_NAME
.Fc
 *SSL_get0_CA_list(const SSL *s);
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CTX_add1_to_CA_list
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_add1_to_CA_list
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const
.Fo STACK_OF
.Fa X509_NAME
.Fc
 *SSL_get0_peer_CA_list(const SSL *s);
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The functions described here set and manage the list of CA names that
are sent between two communicating peers.
.Pp
For TLS versions 1.2 and earlier the list of CA names is only sent from
the server to the client when requesting a client certificate.
So any list of CA names set is never sent from client to server and the
list of CA names retrieved by
.Xr SSL_get0_peer_CA_list 3
is always
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
For TLS 1.3 the list of CA names is sent using the
.Sy certificate_authorities
extension and may be sent by a client (in the ClientHello message) or by
a server (when requesting a certificate).
.Pp
In most cases it is not necessary to set CA names on the client side.
The list of CA names that are acceptable to the client will be sent in
plaintext to the server.
This has privacy implications and may also have performance implications
if the list is large.
This optional capability was introduced as part of TLSv1.3 and therefore
setting CA names on the client side will have no impact if that protocol
version has been disabled.
Most servers do not need this and so this should be avoided unless
required.
.Pp
The "client CA list" functions below only have an effect when called on
the server side.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list
sets the
.Fa list
of CAs sent to the client when requesting a client certificate for
.Fa ctx .
Ownership of
.Fa list
is transferred to
.Fa ctx
and it should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_set_client_CA_list
sets the
.Fa list
of CAs sent to the client when requesting a client certificate for the
chosen
.Fa ssl ,
overriding the setting valid for
.Fa ssl Ns 's
SSL_CTX object.
Ownership of
.Fa list
is transferred to
.Fa s
and it should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_get_client_CA_list 3
returns the list of client CAs explicitly set for
.Fa ctx
using
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list .
The returned list should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get_client_CA_list 3
returns the list of client CAs explicitly set for
.Fa ssl
using
.Fn SSL_set_client_CA_list
or
.Fa ssl Ns 's
SSL_CTX object with
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list ,
when in server mode.
In client mode, SSL_get_client_CA_list returns the list of client CAs
sent from the server, if any.
The returned list should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_add_client_CA 3
adds the CA name extracted from
.Sy cacert
to the list of CAs sent to the client when requesting a client
certificate for
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Xr SSL_add_client_CA 3
adds the CA name extracted from
.Sy cacert
to the list of CAs sent to the client when requesting a client
certificate for the chosen
.Fa ssl ,
overriding the setting valid for
.Fa ssl Ns 's
SSL_CTX object.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get0_peer_CA_list 3
retrieves the list of CA names (if any) the peer has sent.
This can be called on either the server or the client side.
The returned list should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
The "generic CA list" functions below are very similar to the "client CA
list" functions except that they have an effect on both the server and
client sides.
The lists of CA names managed are separate - so you cannot (for example)
set CA names using the "client CA list" functions and then get them
using the "generic CA list" functions.
Where a mix of the two types of functions has been used on the server
side then the "client CA list" functions take precedence.
Typically, on the server side, the "client CA list " functions should be
used in preference.
As noted above in most cases it is not necessary to set CA names on the
client side.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set0_CA_list
sets the list of CAs to be sent to the peer to
.Fa name_list .
Ownership of
.Fa name_list
is transferred to
.Fa ctx
and it should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_set0_CA_list
sets the list of CAs to be sent to the peer to
.Fa name_list
overriding any list set in the parent
.Vt SSL_CTX
of
.Fa s .
Ownership of
.Fa name_list
is transferred to
.Fa s
and it should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_get0_CA_list 3
retrieves any previously set list of CAs set for
.Fa ctx .
The returned list should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get0_CA_list 3
retrieves any previously set list of CAs set for
.Fa s
or if none are set the list from the parent
.Vt SSL_CTX
is retrieved.
The returned list should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_add1_to_CA_list
appends the CA subject name extracted from
.Fa x
to the list of CAs sent to peer for
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn SSL_add1_to_CA_list
appends the CA subject name extracted from
.Fa x
to the list of CAs sent to the peer for
.Fa s ,
overriding the setting in the parent
.Vt SSL_CTX .
.Sh NOTES
When a TLS/SSL server requests a client certificate (see
.Sy SSL_CTX_set_verify(3) Ns ),
it sends a list of CAs, for which it will accept certificates, to the
client.
.Pp
This list must explicitly be set using
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list
or
.Fn SSL_CTX_set0_CA_list
for
.Fa ctx
and
.Fn SSL_set_client_CA_list
or
.Fn SSL_set0_CA_list
for the specific
.Fa ssl .
The list specified overrides the previous setting.
The CAs listed do not become trusted
.Pf ( Fa list
only contains the names, not the complete certificates); use
.Xr SSL_CTX_load_verify_locations 3
to additionally load them for verification.
.Pp
If the list of acceptable CAs is compiled in a file, the
.Xr SSL_load_client_CA_file 3
function can be used to help to import the necessary data.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_add_client_CA 3 ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_add1_to_CA_list ,
.Xr SSL_add_client_CA 3
and
.Fn SSL_add1_to_CA_list
can be used to add additional items the list of CAs.
If no list was specified before using
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_set0_CA_list ,
.Fn SSL_set_client_CA_list
or
.Fn SSL_set0_CA_list ,
a new CA list for
.Fa ctx
or
.Fa ssl
(as appropriate) is opened.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list ,
.Fn SSL_set_client_CA_list ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list ,
.Fn SSL_set_client_CA_list ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_set0_CA_list
and
.Fn SSL_set0_CA_list
do not return a value.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_get_client_CA_list 3 ,
.Xr SSL_get_client_CA_list 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_get0_CA_list 3
and
.Xr SSL_get0_CA_list 3
return a stack of CA names or
.Dv NULL
is no CA names are set.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_add_client_CA(),SSL_add_client_CA 3 ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_add1_to_CA_list
and
.Fn SSL_add1_to_CA_list
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get0_peer_CA_list 3
returns a stack of CA names sent by the peer or
.Dv NULL
or an empty stack if no list was sent.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Scan all certificates in
.Sy CAfile
and list them as acceptable CAs:
.Bd -literal
 SSL_CTX_set_client_CA_list(ctx, SSL_load_client_CA_file(CAfile));
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_load_client_CA_file 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_load_verify_locations 3
